{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1252937-w20-versions","id":1252937,"title":"W20 Versions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-09T21:28:18-07:00","id":1252937,"title":"W20 Versions","content":"I am seeing two versions of W20 out there. So far as I know, I should have the final version, having paid for it, yet I am hearing about a version with alternate rules for certain Gifts, renown rewards. so on. How do I know if I actually have the right version?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T22:43:12-07:00","id":1252966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windthin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1252937-w20-versions#post1252937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am seeing two versions of W20 out there. So far as I know, I should have the final version, having paid for it, yet I am hearing about a version with alternate rules for certain Gifts, renown rewards. so on. How do I know if I actually have the right version?</div> </div> </div> </div>In printed form or PDF?<br /> <br /> Whatever currently downloads from your drivethru library will be the correct version and should match the printed version.<br /> <br /> The other version would be the older download from before errata was applied and the pdf was finalized for print.<br /> <br /> If more than one version was actually printed, then that is weird and I have no idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T02:58:25-07:00","id":1252998,"title":"","content":"Only one version as far as I'm aware in terms of content. Obviously the kickstarter version is physically different to the PoD version but the contents are exactly the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T14:39:14-07:00","id":1254336,"title":"","content":"PDF. I am wondering if some people didn't get a hold of an early version, as is often the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T16:39:36-07:00","id":1254348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windthin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1252937-w20-versions?p=1254336#post1254336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PDF. I am wondering if some people didn't get a hold of an early version, as is often the case.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its possible folks got hold of the backers released pdf and pirated it which would include a few pre-errata rules, but not really enough to call it a different version. There wasn't that much errata for W20 from what I recall as a backer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T16:56:16-07:00","id":1254354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1252937-w20-versions?p=1254348#post1254348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Its possible folks got hold of the backers released pdf and pirated it which would include a few pre-errata rules, but not really enough to call it a different version. There wasn't that much errata for W20 from what I recall as a backer.</div> </div> </div> </div>W20 actually had one of the bigger fixes I've noticed. The first release had two completely different systems for (non-Rage) multiple actions, in different parts of the book. Other than that, I don't think it had the kind of changes OP is describing. The backer version is definitely floating around the pirate scene though, and that one difference is big enough to notice and call out more than most errata changes. That alone could be the source of the confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13544-impeesa","name":"Impeesa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T21:45:42-07:00","id":1254399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Impeesa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1252937-w20-versions?p=1254354#post1254354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W20 actually had one of the bigger fixes I've noticed. The first release had two completely different systems for (non-Rage) multiple actions, in different parts of the book. Other than that, I don't think it had the kind of changes OP is describing. The backer version is definitely floating around the pirate scene though, and that one difference is big enough to notice and call out more than most errata changes. That alone could be the source of the confusion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah...yep forgot about that. I think that must be it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T21:03:11-07:00","id":1257078,"title":"","content":"I've been told of a few Gifts and Rites with variant rules, most notably Troll Skin, diff. 7 in one version, diff. 5 in another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T00:32:58-07:00","id":1257105,"title":"","content":"Hm yeah, Troll Skin is difficulty 7 in the preview release, 5 in the final. Actual functional changes like that are usually pretty rare though, as far as I've seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13544-impeesa","name":"Impeesa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T05:37:42-07:00","id":1257552,"title":"","content":"Okay.<br /> I just got annoyed and did a PDF comparsion.<br /> <br /> Result: mostly typos, some C&amp;P (like in the Performance description of the preview &quot;A player must always choose a speciality in Crafts...&quot;)<br /> <br /> Gifts:<br /> Form Mastery: The part with the intial success for tranformations is gone because this rule does not exist anymore.<br /> Catfeet: 100 feet aren't 91 meters anymore.<br /> Wind Claws: Only works with &quot;natural&quot; attacks.<br /> Curse of Aeolus: &quot;The fog covers roughly one city block in area.&quot;<br /> <br /> Fetishes:<br /> Klaive and Grand Klaive: Silver damage not &quot;unsoakable&quot;. (Breed Form, Lunas Armor and so on...)<br /> Jarlhammer: Difficulty 7 and STR +6 Damage.<br /> <br /> Backgrounds:<br /> Fate is can be raised by XP.<br /> <br /> Splitting Dice Pools as said.<br /> <br /> Form Modifiers:<br /> Crinos is MAN -3<br /> Hispo is MAN -3<br /> Lupus is MAN -3<br /> <br /> Merits and Flaws:<br /> Calm Heart: Rage rolls are at +2 diff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T19:37:53-07:00","id":1296868,"title":"","content":"Interesting. So the diff. 5 one IS the final version. That's the big thing I was hoping to find out. Which was which. Thanks. Those other details are nice also, though I run Calm Heart differently since I feel that the Werewolf version is a poor fit for the game; unlike vampire, you DO want some successes. I made it instead where it takes more successes to frenzy or go Thrall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T07:48:20-07:00","id":1297251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lastlostboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1252937-w20-versions?p=1257552#post1257552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay.<br /> I just got annoyed and did a PDF comparsion.<br /> <br /> Result: mostly typos, some C&amp;P (like in the Performance description of the preview &quot;A player must always choose a speciality in Crafts...&quot;)<br /> <br /> Gifts:<br /> Form Mastery: The part with the intial success for tranformations is gone because this rule does not exist anymore.<br /> Catfeet: 100 feet aren't 91 meters anymore.<br /> Wind Claws: Only works with &quot;natural&quot; attacks.<br /> Curse of Aeolus: &quot;The fog covers roughly one city block in area.&quot;<br /> <br /> Fetishes:<br /> Klaive and Grand Klaive: Silver damage not &quot;unsoakable&quot;. (Breed Form, Lunas Armor and so on...)<br /> Jarlhammer: Difficulty 7 and STR +6 Damage.<br /> <br /> Backgrounds:<br /> Fate is can be raised by XP.<br /> <br /> Splitting Dice Pools as said.<br /> <br /> Form Modifiers:<br /> Crinos is MAN -3<br /> Hispo is MAN -3<br /> Lupus is MAN -3<br /> <br /> Merits and Flaws:<br /> Calm Heart: Rage rolls are at +2 diff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Any other differences ?<br /> Like fixing the melee weapon chart, other fetish weapons, or gifts like razor claw ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 03-17-2019, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T03:39:52-07:00","id":1300226,"title":"","content":"No, that was everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T11:09:33-07:00","id":1300331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lastlostboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1252937-w20-versions?p=1300226#post1300226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that was everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T09:29:19-07:00","id":1305072,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12609_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12609\" data-vbnamecard=\"12609\">lastlostboy</a> Someone told me Grand Klaives do +5 damage in final W20 version, is that true ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T00:32:14-07:00","id":1305924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1252937-w20-versions?p=1305072#post1305072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12609_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12609\" data-vbnamecard=\"12609\">lastlostboy</a> Someone told me Grand Klaives do +5 damage in final W20 version, is that true ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yes, sorry, don't know how I missed that even I've read the paragraph because of the &quot;downgraded&quot; damage.<br /> <br /> &quot;The difficulty to attack with a grand klaive is 7, and it inflicts Strength +5 damage. Werewolves soak this damage as silver (typically, not at all).&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T08:23:40-07:00","id":1306001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lastlostboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1252937-w20-versions?p=1305924#post1305924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, yes, sorry, don't know how I missed that even I've read the paragraph because of the &quot;downgraded&quot; damage.<br /> <br /> &quot;The difficulty to attack with a grand klaive is 7, and it inflicts Strength +5 damage. Werewolves soak this damage as silver (typically, not at all).&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah since lupus an homids don't soak lethal or aggravated damage in breed form at all. The soak silver in breed form thing is applicable only for silver spoons ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T10:23:59-07:00","id":1306035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1252937-w20-versions?p=1306001#post1306001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah since lupus an homids don't soak lethal or aggravated damage in breed form at all. The soak silver in breed form thing is applicable only for silver spoons ...</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't get harmed by it in breedform, though. I mean, yeah, they cannot soak agg-damage. But it isn't -insta- burn.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T02:03:07-07:00","id":1306202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1252937-w20-versions?p=1306035#post1306035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't get harmed by it in breedform, though. I mean, yeah, they cannot soak agg-damage. But it isn't -insta- burn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, they also don't lose Gnosis from contact with silver, the confusing is this ''soak silver thing'', it's so limited it rarely is usable as a rule, by core book standards.<br /> In W20 Changing Ways is mentioned that homids and lupuses soak lethal damage in their breed form which contradicts the core book. That also changes entirely the ''soak silver'' thing, since silver bullets may be soaked in breed form by lupuses and homids. I bet we should keep what suits the mood of our games.<br /> <br /> I vote for the core book rule on soaking silver since it makes silver a real threat not to take lightly, and not a ''I am lupus so I take breed form to soak the rifle shot with 6 dice'' meta-game thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 04-20-2019, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T02:33:22-07:00","id":1306203,"title":"","content":"What do you mean?<br /> <br /> The &quot;unsoakable&quot; vs &quot;silver damage&quot; is a pretty huge deal.<br /> Now you can soak Klaives with armor vests or Lunas Armor gift or Silver Resistance merit and I bet there is a fetish for that too.<br /> Instead of the hurr-durr-unsoakable-bullshit.<br /> <br /> Nothing should ever be &quot;unsoakable&quot;. Make it AGG or make it automatic health levels but never &quot;unsoakable&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T13:14:43-07:00","id":1306318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lastlostboy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1252937-w20-versions?p=1306203#post1306203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean?<br /> <br /> The &quot;unsoakable&quot; vs &quot;silver damage&quot; is a pretty huge deal.<br /> Now you can soak Klaives with armor vests or Lunas Armor gift or Silver Resistance merit and I bet there is a fetish for that too.<br /> Instead of the hurr-durr-unsoakable-bullshit.<br /> <br /> Nothing should ever be &quot;unsoakable&quot;. Make it AGG or make it automatic health levels but never &quot;unsoakable&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well silver damage is unsoakable to garou, not generaly unsoakable, like Balefire is in W20 Book of the Wyrm.<br /> And yes there are ways to soak it, though I don't knowif vests should soak aggravated weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T01:34:05-07:00","id":1306473,"title":"","content":"The point is: the first wording was 'unsoakable'. And it's good they changed it/clear it up.<br /> Because there is no reason Spirits weren't allowed to soak klaives but with &quot;normal&quot; silver swords it was okay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:45:37-07:00","id":1307048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1252937-w20-versions?p=1306202#post1306202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...In W20 Changing Ways is mentioned that homids and lupuses soak lethal damage in their breed form which contradicts the core book. That also changes entirely the ''soak silver'' thing, since silver bullets may be soaked in breed form by lupuses and homids. I bet we should keep what suits the mood of our games. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>W20 Changing Ways, taken as &quot;canon,&quot; creates a LOT of confusion and inconsistencies with the W20 core rules, so if you're going to use it as a source book, do so with caution and make sure to research anything you're planning to use so you can settle the differences before they come up in-game. I don't want to seem overly critical, but my group has found a few inconsistencies within our own hard copies of the W20 core book, where you'll find a different answer to your question, depending on what chapter you're looking in. I don't know when the &quot;errata&quot; someone mentioned above were baked into new printings of the books, so I can't say whether we have pre- or post-errata books, or one of each, but they're definitely officially published hard copies. None of the problems we've found in the W20 core book are as serious as what we've found the Changing Ways book, which in our opinion should have gone through a lot more proofreading and editing before it was published.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T00:38:35-07:00","id":1307165,"title":"","content":"To be fair. The core book is already inconsisting with page 290 reading:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lethal damage can be soaked by Garou and many other supernatural creatures at difficulty 6. Humans cannot normally soak lethal damage, although exceptionally tough ones may be able to try and soak it (Storyteller\u2019s option) at difficulty 8. </div> </div> </div>It's not Changing Ways that gets it wrong. The CRB never got it right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T11:15:53-07:00","id":1307257,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12609_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12609\" data-vbnamecard=\"12609\">lastlostboy</a> what rule you prefer on breed form and lethal soaking ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T12:33:55-07:00","id":1307279,"title":"","content":"The breed form shouldn't be able to soak lethal damage. We never played like this. We consider the breed form perfectly human in every way.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't matter. I just wanted to point out that even the core book got it wrong. (Or right - who knows. -_-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12609,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","user":"lastlostboy","date":". 04-23-2019, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12609-lastlostboy","name":"lastlostboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12609_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T13:44:05-07:00","id":1307293,"title":"","content":"Choices, choices and the choices we make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T03:06:36-07:00","id":1309608,"title":"","content":"I've always run they can soak lethal in breed form. They're not quite human, is the thing. Remember, you can knock one out with lethal and it will survive it and slowly regenerate over time where a human would not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T01:48:57-07:00","id":1309877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windthin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1252937-w20-versions?p=1309608#post1309608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always run they can soak lethal in breed form. They're not quite human, is the thing. Remember, you can knock one out with lethal and it will survive it and slowly regenerate over time where a human would not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou in breed form heal as humans do ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T03:22:28-07:00","id":1309881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1252937-w20-versions?p=1309877#post1309877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Garou in breed form heal as humans do ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they heal much faster. You can get one health level per day of rest even in breed form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T18:04:08-07:00","id":1309961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1252937-w20-versions?p=1309881#post1309881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, they heal much faster. You can get one health level per day of rest even in breed form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Garou dropped to Incap from Lethal revert to breed form but, if they're lupus or homid, have an advanced form of healing that can keep them alive. It's not full regeneration, but it's significantly faster than humans, and they're not going to die from the Lethal like a human will, so if they can crawl off and hide, they have a chance of coming back. It's not one a day, though, it's one every 8 hours, until they regain consciousness and can shift to regenerate more swiftly. The book states they don't soak lethal in breed form, though that can be up to the ST, just as it states that in dramatic situations even humans can potentially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}